WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.068
-In the notes, you thanked
the New York City subway.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.670 line:92%
I have never in my time here

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:06.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
heard anyone say,
"Thank you, subway."

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:06.639 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
So what was it
about the New York City subway

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:11.044 line:92%
that you felt in debt to?

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:13.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I mean --
Okay, and here's --

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like I need
to disclaim by --

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:18.118
You know, I understand if you've
lived here for a long time,

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:21.454
and you've caught the subway
5,000 times, you would hate it.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:21.888 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For me, it still has
a bit of romance.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even though I did get
stuck on it for four hours.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you were on the train
that got stuck for four hours?

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I was.
-That sounded really awful.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sitting on the floor
for four hours.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.866
-Wow! And when you're sitting
on the floor for four hours,

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
does anyone notice
that Lorde is on the train?

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.303 line:92%
-I don't know if they noticed.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
All I could think about
was that I had

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:41.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little oatmeal sachet
in my bag, and I was like,

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:42.876 size:75% position:38% line:92%
if anyone finds out,

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is gonna be,
like, prized commodity.

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:46.513 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:48.114 line:92%
Like, it's gonna be like "Lost."

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.282 line:92%
This will be my family now.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-We're gonna be here forever.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.685
-'Cause, see,
I would've immediately thought,

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, what can I barter
with my oatmeal?"

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:55.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "What can I
get off people?"

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What can you
barter down there, though?

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:58.458 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Like, more food?

00:00:58.458 --> 00:00:59.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would just, like,
raise the price.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:03.063
I would be like, "This usually
is a dollar, but now it's $150."

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You sit on the floor,
give me your seat."

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
-No, but I love the subway.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:08.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like it was really nice
riding this.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.470
I would kind of sit there
and listen to the work,

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it helped me kind of
be around people,

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, 'cause when
you're working in a studio,

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're very isolated
and kind of just hang out

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:17.977 size:88% position:44% line:92%
with a couple of people.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.179 line:92%
So I feel like it sort of

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:21.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
reintroduced me
back into society.

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.750 line:92%
And people would be very sweet.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.584 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They'd kind of --

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
someone would be like...

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.923
and sort of do a little look,
and I'd be like, "Shh, shh."

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:30.723 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I was reading an article
where you were talking --

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
And has this
been your whole life, this --

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.163 size:84% position:42% line:92%
the way you see colors?

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yes.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I guess --
What is it?

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not that you hear --
Explain it for me.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
So, it's called synesthesia,

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:48.541
and, basically, it's like when
the senses overlap in some way.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:51.511 line:92%
So, for me, music and words

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:55.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of have colors
and textures and forms.

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:56.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's like
this weird, abstract thing,

00:01:56.883 --> 00:02:00.820
but making music is, like,
a really visual process for me.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.755 line:92%
-And so, then, is that how --

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you describe
your music in colors?

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, if you were
talking to Jack,

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you say, like,
"This is a little too..."

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:12.899
-Yeah, I try hard to keep
the color things away from,

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.000 line:92%
like, synesthesia muggles

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.468 size:84% position:42%
'cause they feel, like,
it's super-annoying,

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:18.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I would definitely like --
I would kind of --

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:19.472 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.608 line:92%
I would slip and be, like...

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:23.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
"It just doesn't
look very nice,"

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:24.077 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and he would be like,

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:26.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What do you want me
to do with that information?"

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:29.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "I can't --
There's nothing there."

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:33.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What would you say
are the colors of this album?

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:34.020 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Oh, well. They, uh --

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.221 line:92%
They are the colors of the --

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:38.491
A lot of the color's in the
actual cover painting itself,

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.393 line:92%
so it's violets and blues.

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:41.060 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-The cover is beautiful.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.396
And after I read that, I sort of
looked at the album art

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:45.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
and having listened
to some of the songs,

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:45.899 line:92%
I had a real understanding.

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:48.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
Again, and I'm a muggle,
I'll admit, but...

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:49.369 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:50.403 line:92%
It did make total sense to me.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I will say,
you really nailed it,

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
if those were the colors
you were looking for.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:54.641 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:55.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'm just so happy
to have you here,

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
and thank you so much for
singing a song off the album.

00:02:57.944 --> 00:02:58.511 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We can't wait.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
What a pleasure for me.

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Give it up for Lorde,
everybody.

